<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sauromates II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 174–210 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Tiberius Julius Sauromates II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> Julius Sauromates II was king of the Bosporan Kingdom from about 174 to 210 CE, ruling as a client of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Inscriptions credit him with victories over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraces">Siraces</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tauri">Tauri</a> and with making the sea safe for shipping. His long reign was a time of relative prosperity for the cities of the Bosporus, the high point of the kingdom's Roman period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sauromates-ii.jpg" alt="Sauromates II" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Odysses · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiberius_Julius_Sauromates_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
